2m - kb &= \log{(10)^{2kb}}\\
2m &= kb + 2kb\\
m &= \frac{kb + 2kb}{2}\\
m &= 2kb
\end{align*}

Now we can set the two expressions for $m$ equal to each other:
\begin{align*}
\frac{n\ \log{15} - 1}{2} &= 2kb\\
n\ \log{15} - 1 &= 4kb\\
n\ \log{15} &= 4kb + 1
\end{align*}

We can solve for $n$ by dividing both sides of the equation by $\log{15}$:
